  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-03 (concurrent run stage 2, same branch as WI-mujod, NOT merged, no status change). Branch jgstern-agent/fix/mujod, commit ad7cde0712. Fixed in io_boundary.module_hint_disjuncts, the one spelling expansion behind the row choice (named_lookup_arm, io + taint) and the coverage gate: a CLOSED table _CXX_C_LIBRARY_HEADERS (28: [headers] cassert..cwctype, the five C++17-deprecated, C++26 cstdbit/cstdckdint) gives a C++ C-library header its C stem as a spelling. No rows duplicated. SCOPED to calls in c/cpp (language threaded through named_lookup_arm / prefer_exact_owner / _module_hint_candidates; io passes the catalogue's language, taint the callee's, the gate catalog.language) because Python's cmath is not math and python declares math complete. Report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/mujod.md.\nEVIDENCE: filed fixture shape, verify-claims host_secret->network inconclusive rc 2 -> violated rc 1 (stdlib.getenv -> sys/socket.sendto). test_cxx_c_library_header_spelling.py (23 tests; mutating the language scope to `if True` reds the 4 scope tests). Corpus, C/C++ surveyed under both trees: survey edge sets unchanged on all 10 C/C++ repos; tagged call sites +4 modsecurity, +102 whisper.cpp, +44 powerdns, +73 sherpa-onnx, 0 on the 6 C repos. Stated loosening: a C++ disjunct whose C stem is audited complete (errno, stdint, stdbool, stddef, stdarg, limits, float, inttypes, ctype, math) now counts as enumerated. Residuals reached from C++ now, pre-existing in C: printf/putchar fs_write (filed WI-sofam-mazof-havid-bisij-manod-zonak-tozis-tunod), fprintf(stderr) on the fs_write row, ADL getline(ifs, line) reported as stdio.getline (boundary right)."  # 45b8
